            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0196" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.008 North Pacific/315: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-25T18:00:00-05:00">March 25, 1938—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>105. Your No. 201, March 25, 2 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The revised draft press communiqué is acceptable and release will be made
                        at 10:30 p.m. this evening Eastern Standard Time for tomorrow morning’s
                        papers.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>With reference to your paragraph 6 the Department authorizes confirmation
                        with regard to the character of the Japanese undertaking by informal letter
                        as suggested. The text of the letter should adhere to the sense of and
                        perhaps refer to the final paragraph of the revised draft communiqué.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I desire to commend and to express appreciation of the painstaking and
                        effective efforts of the Embassy in the difficult negotiations just
                        concluded. I also authorize you in your discretion to convey orally to the
                        Minister for Foreign Affairs and Mr. Yoshizawa an expression of appreciation
                        of their sincere and helpful collaboration.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
